...first post also....

Hoorah! I made it! To be honest, it was much easier than I had
expected. I had really been fixated on doing a monk for my first
ascension ever, but would continually get frustrated with silly things
(mostly my infatuation with chaotic monks wielding stormbringer and
wandering around haphazardly.)

I finally decided to try something easier, so I went in, heavily
spoiled with a Valk named after my wife's maiden name. The dungeon
(RNG?) was very good to me. Every other level had a sink or an altar. I
also had the benefit of several stores along the way that were stocked
pretty well. I got a couple of wishes and picked up GDSM and power
gauntlets to go along with the Mjollnir that I had been granted. Mines
had an amulet. Somewheres along the line I became permanently invisible
so I carried wrapping for the occasional visit to the store.

I think I would've been super extra prepared had it not been for a
really crazy accident involving a newly found bag, the bag of holding
with many of my goodies and a chest that I was trying to move stuff
into. While fumbling around and not thinking about it, something went
where it wasn't supposed to go and poof!

It took my wish wand, my death wand, several potions and scrolls, rings
and amulets and a few other things I don't quite remember. To make
matters worse, when I ran into a mindflayer a few levels later, panic
somehow overtook me and I spent a turn getting my brain eaten before
teleporting him away and using Mjollnir from a distance. Only after it
was dead did I notice that I kept my blessed genocide scroll in my main
inventory after all. So the mindflayer was bad, but what was worse is
the fact that I forgot my way around and I couldn't remember the names
of any of my rings.

Out of frustration, I decided to forge on. I still had a pretty good
set of equipment. A magic lamp yielded me a magic marker and I was able
to bless and enchant everything I had pretty well. Forgot that I
should've written myself a new charging scroll though so I didn't quite
get as much use as I could have.

At one point I fell through a trap door, found the up stair and was
standing on a statue of perseus. I figured I was on medusa's level so I
spoiled myself for a little bit on the internet, before realizing that
I had come from the opposite direction and I was standing next to her.
I stayed invisible and beat the heck out of her with Mjollnir. Got a
shield of reflection.

Gehennom was real boring. Conrad was pretty yolked out to the point
that nothing could hurt her much, especially with the orb safely in
hand. Killed the wizard and learned all about annoyance as I would get
sucked back down 3 levels seemingly every time I went from 46-45.

Finally made it out and up. Wizard only bothered me one other time, but
I had picked up another death wand somewheres.

The planes were easy with a ring of conflict although I did go through
an amulet getting sucked in by an air elemental. When I got to the
altars, I took a guess at the center one. Teleported everybody out of
the way and I had figured right.

So now, I figure I'll really try for my monk. Also I want to try and
get a pet gremlin. I had a gang of them briefly and I was hoping to
really live up to being the War horseman of the apocalypse with an army
of gremlins (a la a post I had read on here some time ago), but alas a
priest of moloch made quick work of them before I could get in my own
shots at him.

